        ],
        "principlesCheck": "Self-check only. Same whole-method as Q6: distance formula, square both sides, expand, collect, divide by 2 to a monic quadratic, PSF, null factor law. Both coordinate differences contain $k$. Roots 1 and -5 are distinct and admissible. I verified both roots against the original distance: each gives $\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}$. No new teaching, cue, scaffold or diagram. No ratings or acceptance claimed."
